1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,769
Hi, I'm Surekha Jaknalli, from team Impromptu, with Rahul Rajpoot and Vivek Chaturvedi.

2
00:00:05,769 --> 00:00:12,068
This is my part of our work: Task Harness, a reusable quality gate for every AI call at Hyland.

3
00:00:12,068 --> 00:00:18,103
In the next few minutes, I'll show the problem, the solution, a live demo, and the results.

4
00:00:18,903 --> 00:00:26,179
When teams ask a generative AI model to read a document, it is usually right, but sometimes it is quietly wrong.

5
00:00:26,179 --> 00:00:32,221
In our test, the cheapest Claude model got 6 out of 30 invoices wrong, and nobody was warned.

6
00:00:32,221 --> 00:00:36,899
For example, it wrote a discount as minus 393 point 32, instead of plus.

7
00:00:36,899 --> 00:00:41,317
A finance system would add that discount, instead of subtracting it.

8
00:00:41,317 --> 00:00:46,515
Even the most expensive model returned 15 of its 30 answers in the wrong format.

9
00:00:46,515 --> 00:00:52,427
So today, teams either trust the AI blindly, or pay for the biggest model, just to be safe.

10
00:00:53,227 --> 00:00:56,136
Task Harness puts a supervisor around the AI.

11
00:00:56,136 --> 00:00:58,593
A versioned template defines the task.

12
00:00:58,593 --> 00:01:00,662
Normal code cleans the document.

13
00:01:00,662 --> 00:01:01,632
The AI answers.

14
00:01:01,632 --> 00:01:04,024
Then simple code checks every answer.

15
00:01:04,024 --> 00:01:08,938
If a check fails, the AI gets one retry, with the exact problem as feedback.

16
00:01:08,938 --> 00:01:12,689
If it still fails, the answer goes to a person for review.

17
00:01:12,689 --> 00:01:16,374
It is never passed on silently, and every step is logged.

18
00:01:17,174 --> 00:01:19,605
The checks are plain code, not more AI.

19
00:01:19,605 --> 00:01:21,974
Is every value really in the document?

20
00:01:21,974 --> 00:01:27,646
Is it from the right line: not the due date, not the customer, not a purchase order number?

21
00:01:27,646 --> 00:01:28,830
Do the sums add up?

22
00:01:28,830 --> 00:01:32,383
And is the format exactly what downstream systems expect?

23
00:01:33,183 --> 00:01:35,606
We checked what already exists at Hyland.

24
00:01:35,606 --> 00:01:38,679
Brainware already validates classic invoice capture.

25
00:01:38,679 --> 00:01:46,123
An internal prompt optimizer improves prompt wording, and several proofs of concept extract fields with large language models.

26
00:01:46,123 --> 00:01:52,150
But none of them check generative AI answers in a standard way, or measure which model is good enough.

27
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:54,218
That is the gap Task Harness fills.

28
00:01:54,218 --> 00:01:58,709
Invoices are simply our test case, because their answers are easy to verify.

29
00:01:59,509 --> 00:02:00,940
Here is the working app.

30
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:07,141
On the Try it screen, I run an invoice through the full harness, and the six stages light up one by one.

31
00:02:07,141 --> 00:02:10,242
On its first attempt, the AI broke the format rules.

32
00:02:10,242 --> 00:02:14,774
The harness caught it, sent feedback, and the AI fixed it on the second try.

33
00:02:14,774 --> 00:02:17,338
Every field now matches the correct answer.

34
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:23,340
If I paste text that is not an invoice, the harness does not accept a made-up answer.

35
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:27,319
It sends it for human review, and explains why, in plain English.

36
00:02:28,119 --> 00:02:30,753
Side by side shows the same invoice twice.

37
00:02:30,753 --> 00:02:35,269
On the left, the AI alone: the discount is wrong, and nobody was warned.

38
00:02:35,269 --> 00:02:36,712
That is a silent error.

39
00:02:36,712 --> 00:02:43,110
On the right, the same cheap model inside the harness: every field is correct, and every check passed.

40
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:45,910
And it is not only for invoices.

41
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:48,035
A new task is just a new template.

42
00:02:48,035 --> 00:02:51,659
Here, Key facts from any text summarises a customer email.

43
00:02:51,659 --> 00:02:58,221
Every key point must come with an exact quote, and names, dates and numbers are checked against the text.

44
00:02:59,021 --> 00:03:03,912
Here are the results on 30 invoices, using Claude on Hyland's AWS account.

45
00:03:03,912 --> 00:03:10,719
The cheapest model with the harness got 30 out of 30 correct, with 0 format errors and 0 silent errors.

46
00:03:10,719 --> 00:03:17,592
That is 2.6 times faster, and about 38 times cheaper, than the most expensive model with a plain prompt.

47
00:03:18,392 --> 00:03:23,753
Next, this becomes a template library that any team can extend without prompt engineering.

48
00:03:23,753 --> 00:03:32,509
It can run as a check after every call on Hyland's AI gateway, keep an audit trail, and help each team pick the cheapest model that is good enough.

49
00:03:32,509 --> 00:03:39,061
It also fits our own tools: for example, checking that Impromptu's prompt rewrites never lose or invent facts.

50
00:03:39,861 --> 00:03:49,040
To be honest about the limits: this is 30 synthetic invoices and two tasks so far, and the general text checks verify facts, not the full meaning.

51
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:56,396
Our ask is one pilot team with real, approved documents, time with the Brainware and AI gateway teams, and a sponsor.

52
00:03:56,396 --> 00:04:01,299
Task Harness: checked AI answers, with the cheapest model that is good enough.

53
00:04:01,299 --> 00:04:01,928
Thank you.
